# Git Notes — What I Learned Today

## 1. Git Basic Workflow

Git mainly works with these areas:

```text
Working Directory
       ↓
   git add
       ↓
  Staging Area
       ↓
 git commit
       ↓
 Local Repository
```

---

## 2. Initialize a Git Repository

Create a Git repository in the current directory:

```bash
git init
```

---

## 3. Check Repository Status

To see the current status of files:

```bash
git status
```

It shows whether files are:

- Untracked
- Modified
- Staged
- Ready to commit

---

## 4. Add Files to Staging Area

Add a specific file:

```bash
git add index.txt
```

Add all files:

```bash
git add .
```

The `.` means all changes in the current directory.

---

## 5. Commit Changes

Create a commit:

```bash
git commit -m "3 files committing in first round"
```

The `-m` option is used to provide the commit message.

Example:

```bash
git commit -m "Initial commit"
```

---

# Git Diff Commands

## 6. `git diff`

To see the difference between:

```text
Working Directory ↔ Staging Area
```

use:

```bash
git diff
```

This shows changes that have been made but are **not yet staged**.

---

## 7. `git diff --cached`

To see the difference between:

```text
Staging Area ↔ Last Commit
```

use:

```bash
git diff --cached
```

You can also use:

```bash
git diff --staged
```

Both are used to view staged changes.

---

## 8. Compare Working Directory with Last Commit

To compare the current working directory with the latest commit:

```bash
git diff HEAD
```

For a specific file:

```bash
git diff HEAD -- index.txt
```

This compares:

```text
Working Directory + Staging Area
              ↕
            HEAD
```

---

## 9. Compare Staged Changes with Last Commit

To compare the staging area with the latest commit:

```bash
git diff --cached HEAD
```

For a specific file:

```bash
git diff --cached HEAD -- index.txt
```

---

# Comparing Commits

## 10. Compare Two Commits

To see the difference between two specific commits:

```bash
git diff commit1 commit2
```

Example:

```bash
git diff abc123 def456
```

---

## 11. Compare Two Branches

To see the difference between two branches:

```bash
git diff master test
```

This compares the `master` branch with the `test` branch.

---

## 12. Compare Local and Remote Branches

To compare a local branch with a remote branch:

```bash
git diff master origin/master
```

---

# Git Log

## 13. View Commit History

To see the commit history:

```bash
git log
```

For a short one-line version:

```bash
git log --oneline
```

This gives a compact list of commits and their commit IDs.

---

# Removing Files

## 14. Delete a File from Working Directory

Normal Linux command:

```bash
rm index.txt
```

After deleting the file, Git will show the deletion when you run:

```bash
git status
```

---

## 15. Remove a File Using Git

To remove a file from the working directory and stage the deletion:

```bash
git rm index.txt
```

Then commit the change:

```bash
git commit -m "Remove index.txt"
```

---

## 16. Remove a File Only from Staging

If you want to remove a file from the staging area but keep the file in your working directory:

```bash
git rm --cached index.txt
```

Then check:

```bash
git status
```

The file remains on your computer but is no longer tracked/staged by Git.

---

# Checking Tracked Files

## 17. View Files Tracked by Git

To see the files currently tracked by Git:

```bash
git ls-files
```

---

# Working with Staging Area

## 18. Check Staged Files

Use:

```bash
git status
```

Example workflow:

```bash
git add .
git status
git commit -m "Add files"
```

---

# File States in Git

A file generally moves through these stages:

```text
Untracked
    ↓
git add
    ↓
Staged
    ↓
git commit
    ↓
Committed
```

If a tracked file is modified:

```text
Committed
    ↓
File modified
    ↓
Working Directory
    ↓
git add
    ↓
Staging Area
    ↓
git commit
    ↓
Repository
```

---

# Important Difference Between Git Diff Commands

| Command | What it compares |
|---|---|
| `git diff` | Working Directory ↔ Staging Area |
| `git diff --cached` | Staging Area ↔ Last Commit |
| `git diff --staged` | Staging Area ↔ Last Commit |
| `git diff HEAD` | Working Directory + Staging Area ↔ Last Commit |
| `git diff --cached HEAD` | Staging Area ↔ Last Commit |
| `git diff commit1 commit2` | Two commits |
| `git diff master test` | Two branches |
| `git diff master origin/master` | Local branch ↔ Remote branch |

