# Basic Git Workflow — Quick Revision

```bash
# Create repository
git init

# Check status
git status

# Add a file
git add index.txt

# Add all files
git add .

# Check staged changes
git diff --cached

# Commit
git commit -m "Initial commit"

# View commit history
git log --oneline

# Check unstaged changes
git diff

# Compare with latest commit
git diff HEAD

# Remove a file
git rm index.txt

# Remove file from Git but keep it locally
git rm --cached index.txt

# See tracked files
git ls-files
```

---

# Git Mental Model

```text
             git add
Working -----------------> Staging
   |                         |
   |                         |
   |                         | git commit
   |                         ↓
   |                      Repository
   |
   | git diff
   ↓
Changes
```

**Remember:**

```text
git diff
    → What changed but is NOT staged?

git diff --cached
    → What is staged but NOT committed?

git diff HEAD
    → What is different from the last commit?

git status
    → What is the current state of my repository?

git log --oneline
    → What commits have I made?
```
